     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand it's intentional and that you're taking responsibility for it. But 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication where it's appropriate. The extra dose adds substantial risk of GI hemorrhage, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It has no known added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because the effect plateaus at lower doses. I'm not comfortable placing an order with that risk profile.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a GI protection note if you want it\n- Ibuprofen 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours\n- A multimodal regimen, for example ibuprofen plus scheduled acetaminophen, if the goal is stronger analgesia\n\nIf you need the higher dose for a specific reason, such as a protocol or a trial, you can enter it directly in the order system. It would then go through the normal pharmacy verification and override process. I'm glad to help with the order note or the alternatives."
      }
